            <title>[LU-20975] sanityn test_90: open/create and unlink striped directory hangs, session TIMEOUT</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20975</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Session &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/6e3dc6fa-9687-40bb-a2c7-edaa316acc59" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/6e3dc6fa-9687-40bb-a2c7-edaa316acc59&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
(review-dne-zfs-part-5, build 133644) reports sanityn test_90 TIMEOUT.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The subtest log (test set &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7fb2b302-f22b-4719-a422-b0ee1e8206d9" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/7fb2b302-f22b-4719-a422-b0ee1e8206d9&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br/&gt;
shows test_90 start its two background processes ("open/create under&lt;br/&gt;
striped directory" and "unlink striped directory") at 14:39:44 and&lt;br/&gt;
then nothing further: no PASS, no FAIL, no further suite progress.&lt;br/&gt;
The suite log ends there too. The session's own timeout fired later&lt;br/&gt;
(228 minutes), by which time a later suite (recovery-small) was&lt;br/&gt;
running, so the session's "last suite running" does not name sanityn:&lt;br/&gt;
sanityn itself hung in test_90.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This test and error are rare: Rainshadow shows only one other&lt;br/&gt;
occurrence in the last 30 days (Janitor, 2026-09-17, a CRASH rather&lt;br/&gt;
than a TIMEOUT) and no open ticket covers it. A JIRA search for&lt;br/&gt;
"sanityn test_90" and for "open/create and unlink striped directory"&lt;br/&gt;
finds only &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-5344" title="ldlm/ifind deadlock for striped directory" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-5344"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-5344&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, an unrelated striped-directory deadlock resolved&lt;br/&gt;
in 2015.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The patch under test (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12669" title="FLR-EC: recover data from parity code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12669"&gt;LU-12669&lt;/a&gt;) only touches lustre/include/cl_object.h,&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/llite/file.c, lustre/lov/lov_io.c, lustre/obdclass/cl_io.c and&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/tests/sanity-ec.sh: an EC parity-read path with no connection to&lt;br/&gt;
DNE striped directory create/unlink.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69392-ps2-f06d1f5a7c18 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
